  "intro": "A circle of radius $r$ has area $\\pi r^2$ and circumference $2\\pi r$. A central angle of $\\theta$ degrees cuts an arc of length $\\frac{\\theta}{360}\\cdot 2\\pi r$ and a sector of area $\\frac{\\theta}{360}\\cdot\\pi r^2$. An inscribed angle is half the central angle subtending the same arc. The equation of a circle with center $(h,k)$ and radius $r$ is $(x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2$; completing the square converts a general form to this.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "Find the arc length of a $90^\\circ$ arc in a circle of radius $8$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Arc length is $\\frac{\\theta}{360}\\cdot 2\\pi r$.",
          "$\\frac{90}{360}\\cdot 2\\pi(8)=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16\\pi=4\\pi$."
        ],
        "answer": "$4\\pi$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Find the area of a $90^\\circ$ sector in a circle of radius $6$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Sector area is $\\frac{\\theta}{360}\\cdot\\pi r^2$.",
          "$\\frac{90}{360}\\cdot\\pi(36)=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 36\\pi=9\\pi$."
        ],
        "answer": "$9\\pi$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Give the center and radius of $(x-2)^2+(y+3)^2=16$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Compare to $(x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2$.",
          "Center is $(2,-3)$ and $r^2=16$ so $r=4$."
        ],
        "answer": "Center $(2,-3)$, radius $4$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
